  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## What listeners single out\n\n- **Box of Rain** (1 review, 1 other source): Reviewer says it was the first Box of Rain since Phil Lesh died in 2024; Uploader notes Box of Rain was played for the first time since Phil Lesh's 2024 passing, as part of his tribute [1][3]\n\n## Setlist highlights\n\n- **Minglewood Blues**: rare: 11 archived performances [5]\n- **Dead Forever Video Clip**: earliest performance in the archive; rare: 3 archived performances [5]\n- **Box of Rain**: back after 90 archived shows (1005 days); rare: 11 archived performances [5]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **deadco2025-03-22** (recommended): source not stated; 20 songs; 166 min; rated 2.5/5 by 2 [1]\n- **deadco2025-03-22.Rainbowtoez.Shell**: source not stated; 20 songs; 139 min [2]. Said about its sound: Technical problems made the mics cut out, leaving some songs missing or incomplete; uploader's quick mix was made on AirPods [2]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- Stage talk about: Crowd 2nd Set [1]\n- The show included a tribute to the late Phil Lesh [3]\n- Lineup listed: Bobby Weir on rhythm guitar, Mickey Hart on percussion, John Mayer on lead guitar, Oteil Burbridge on bass [1]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **deadco2025-03-22**: taped by Stella Dew; transferred by Stella Dew; source: Zoom iQ7 > iPhone [1]. Also: Recorded with a Zoom iQ7 into an iPhone 11, then WAV, Audacity, and FLAC [1]\n- **deadco2025-03-22.Rainbowtoez.Shell**: taped by Rainbowtoez; transferred by Hunter S II; source: Channels 1 & 2: Shure MoveMic 2 > Bluetooth MOTIV Audio > iPhone 12 [2]. Also: Shure MoveMic 2 mics over Bluetooth MOTIV into an iPhone 12, then WAV, Reaper, and 24-bit FLAC [2]",
